From cdc4239923506f05b12bff15f19e2229623a1b77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:14:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] FlyWeb 3.2.0 interface: Titin's toolbar, tab and bookmark
 icons

Icons converted from Titin's SVGs with softmac FlyWeb/tools/svg2icon.py
(regenerated by FlyWeb/tools/iconos-3.2.0.sh), one common scale keeping
the proportions drawn in Illustrator, calibrated so the back arrow keeps
its current size (12 dip on the 20 dip grid).

Chromium 156 shows the "old" icons (IsRoundedIconsEnabled() is off), so
those are replaced through brave/vector_icons/<same path>: back, forward,
reload, stop, bookmark star (empty and filled), extensions, downloads,
app menu, tab close and the bookmark bar overflow chevron.

Three icons are FlyWeb's own (app/vector_icons) and used only where the
design asks for them, because the Chromium ones are generic or Brave
draws a PNG:
- new tab "+" (hook in horizontal_tab_strip_region_view.cc),
- tab search chevron (hook in tab_strip_combo_button.cc),
- bookmark folder, now a flat vector in kColorBookmarkFolderIcon
  instead of Brave's PNG folders with a gradient.
The Shields outline icon is added for the next change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MwmK2juPkbC58kEi4QFeyU
